    {
      "id": "claim_4ac72bee9d4c4141832fcc92bc17a0ba",
      "statement": "Three untracked files split configuration by review surface: `config.toml` configures the running deployment and names the other two via `identity_file` and `policy_file`, `identity.toml` maps platform accounts onto one `person_id`, and `policy.toml` grants — deny-by-default — who may talk to her and where; all are read once at startup (a live edit changes nothing without a recreate) and secrets stay in the host environment, referenced by variable name.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L114-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d28a4d06eb491fbe73a49e79dd831bbfcc77499b1edca7aedac57cb0eac302e:"
