    {
      "id": "claim_11b32ef9c9a64a03b6647d16f5ba4b69",
      "statement": "A test directory names what makes a test true rather than what it is about — unit tests stand on fakes, contract suites run one suite against many implementations of a port, integration tests go through the real composition root, infra tests need the real backend, and architecture tests read a property off the AST — and a class standing in for a `nora/domain/ports.py` port lives in `nora/testing/`, parametrized into that port's contract suite.",
      "evidence": [
